# A whole SQL query after a pipe gets the same rewrite help as at the start of a query.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | SELECT a FROM t
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..20
  PIPELINE@0..19
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    ERROR@4..19
      IDENT@4..10 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@10..11 " "
      IDENT@11..12 "a"
      WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
      IDENT@13..17 "FROM"
      WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
      IDENT@18..19 "t"
  WHITESPACE@19..20 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `SELECT ... FROM` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:5
  |
1 | t | SELECT a FROM t
  |     ^^^^^^   ---- in DataScript the table comes first
  |     |
  |     this is SQL
  |
  = help: start with the table and pipe it into operators: `t | project a`
